From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:16:22 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 37/43] doc: fomu_evt_header and the libgpiod iCE40 SRAM load

The board in boards.yml (Memory NT: not tried on hardware), the libgpiod
cable's SPI load in cable.yml, and a section in the Lattice page: the
wiring, the command, what is done to the flash, and the checks.

It says plainly that the load is untested on hardware and that libgpiod
may well not reach the iCE40's 1 MHz minimum slave configuration clock
(on a Pi 3 very likely not), in which case it stops with the rate and the
iCE40 boots its flash again. It says what SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP do, that
SIGKILL leaves the iCE40 unconfigured until a power cycle, and how a
caller sets a time limit (timeout -k, never -s KILL).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
